sentences.text:
Basically only three facts need to be established by  the claimants for assessing compensation in the case of  death :-
 (a) age of the deceased; (b) income of the deceased;
 and the (c) the number of dependents.

The issues to  be determined by the Tribunal to arrive at the loss of  dependency are (i) additions/deductions to be made for  arriving at the income; (ii) the deduction to be made MACT NO:104/2019 Meena Devi v. Anurag P.No 8. Of 23 BK  :9:
 towards the personal living expenses of the deceased;
 and (iii) the multiplier to be applied with reference of  the age of the deceased.
